can we use transaction in private method
-> will not work on private method because transaction internally using AOP proxy to apply the transaction on target method
if we define private that wont visible by proxy


ex -> suppose the class is Account

public class AccountService{


@Transactional
public transfer(){

//some logic
}



@Transactional
private doSomething(){
 //some logic
}

}



what this @Transactional do intenally it uses AOP proxy ,  it creates the proxy class that extend the target class in this case 
target clas is AccountService a it as the method which is annoted with @Transactional 

public class AccountServiceProxy extends AccountService{

private AccountService target;
 
 //constructor parametezied
 
 // need to override the method 
 @override
 public void transfer(){
 try{
 	//begin txn
 	target.transfer()
 
 }catch(Exception e){
 
 // rollback 
 }
 
 }
  //if we define  method as private then it is not visible to private class we are not able to override it


}

